  "id": "COMPOUND:41085 - PROTEIN:5840",
  "verbalization": "Prenylagaramide A appears to exert its biological effects through a shared mechanism involving Phosphodiesterase 6C, which is targeted by multiple compounds, including Pronuciferine, Vitetrifolin B, and Pentadecanoate. All three of these substances have a common target, H9, suggesting that they may act through a similar pathway to modulate H9 activity. The evidence indicates that Prenylagaramide A, through its interaction with Phosphodiesterase 6C, may influence H9 function, potentially by altering intracellular signaling or enzyme activity. The consistent targeting of Phosphodiesterase 6C by these compounds supports the hypothesis that Prenylagaramide A could also act on this enzyme to affect H9. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Prenylagaramide A in modulating H9 activity through a shared target, underscoring the importance of Phosphodiesterase 6C in this relationship.",
